const APPLE_PROJECT_EN={"title": "Apple: Financial Forecasting & Equity Valuation", "summary": "A group project linking Apple’s business model and historical financial analysis with FY2026 fourth-quarter and full-year forecasts, FY2027–FY2032 projections and equity valuation. The team uses discounted flow to equity, residual income and relative valuation to compare results under different assumptions and examine terminal value, the cost of equity and market pricing. Deliverables include an English report and an Excel workbook retaining assumptions, forecasts and valuation calculations.", "role": "I prepared the income statement forecasts and related assumptions within Task 3. I combined FY2026 first-three-quarter actuals with the group’s fourth-quarter forecast to establish the full-year base, then built FY2027–FY2032 revenue forecasts by principal product category and Services. Drawing on historical performance and business context, I set assumptions for growth, product and Services margins, R&D, SG&A, taxation and diluted shares, explaining changes in revenue mix, profitability and EPS. These income statement outputs support the team’s subsequent balance sheet forecasts and valuation. The complete report and overall valuation conclusions are group outputs.", "story": [["Connecting business analysis, forecasts and valuation", "The team starts with Apple’s products, Services and ecosystem, connecting financial performance and value drivers to quarterly and annual forecasts. Different equity valuation methods test market pricing. The report presents forecast assumptions, valuation differences and sensitivity analysis together, rather than relying on one headline estimate."], ["Forecasting from product revenue and margin assumptions", "I prepared the income statement forecasts and assumptions, modelling major product categories and Services separately before applying margins, R&D, SG&A, taxation and share-count assumptions. The workbook retains Revenue Build, Annual IS Forecast, IS Assumptions and income statement outputs for subsequent forecasts. The analysis explains revenue and EPS changes over FY2027–FY2032."], ["An individual contribution within the group valuation framework", "The final English report and Excel model cover discounted flow to equity, residual income, relative valuation and market comparisons. My contribution centres on income statement forecasts and assumptions; balance sheet projections, valuation and recommendations are supported by the team’s combined work. Original submission files are retained. HOLD is the group’s course-case conclusion at the report’s research date and under its stated assumptions."]]};
const APPLE_TRANSLATIONS={"苹果公司财务预测与股权估值": "Apple: Financial Forecasting & Equity Valuation", "以苹果公司为对象，将商业模式与历史财务分析、FY2026 第四季度及全年预测、FY2027—FY2032 财务预测与股权估值连接起来。小组采用股权现金流折现、剩余收益及相对估值方法，比较不同假设下的估值结果，讨论终值、资本成本与市场定价之间的关系。成果包括英文估值报告与保留假设、预测和估值计算的 Excel 工作簿。": "A group project linking Apple’s business model and historical financial analysis with FY2026 fourth-quarter and full-year forecasts, FY2027–FY2032 projections and equity valuation. The team uses discounted flow to equity, residual income and relative valuation to compare results under different assumptions and examine terminal value, the cost of equity and market pricing. Deliverables include an English report and an Excel workbook retaining assumptions, forecasts and valuation calculations.", "负责 Task 3 中利润表预测及相关假设分析，将 FY2026 前三季度实际业绩与小组第四季度预测衔接，形成全年利润表预测基础，并按主要产品类别与 Services 构建 FY2027—FY2032 收入预测。结合历史表现与业务背景，设置收入增速、产品及服务毛利率、研发与销售管理费用、税率和稀释股数等假设，解释收入结构、利润率及 EPS 的变化。相关利润表输出供小组后续资产负债表预测与估值使用；完整报告及整体估值结论为小组共同成果。": "I prepared the income statement forecasts and related assumptions within Task 3. I combined FY2026 first-three-quarter actuals with the group’s fourth-quarter forecast to establish the full-year base, then built FY2027–FY2032 revenue forecasts by principal product category and Services. Drawing on historical performance and business context, I set assumptions for growth, product and Services margins, R&D, SG&A, taxation and diluted shares, explaining changes in revenue mix, profitability and EPS. These income statement outputs support the team’s subsequent balance sheet forecasts and valuation. The complete report and overall valuation conclusions are group outputs.", "把企业分析、财务预测与估值连成一条路径": "Connecting business analysis, forecasts and valuation", "小组从苹果的产品、服务与生态系统出发，结合财务表现和价值驱动因素，建立季度及年度预测，再用不同股权估值方法检验市场定价。报告将预测依据、估值差异与敏感性分析一起呈现，避免只给出单一估值数字。": "The team starts with Apple’s products, Services and ecosystem, connecting financial performance and value drivers to quarterly and annual forecasts. Different equity valuation methods test market pricing. The report presents forecast assumptions, valuation differences and sensitivity analysis together, rather than relying on one headline estimate.", "以分产品收入及利润率假设支持预测": "Forecasting from product revenue and margin assumptions", "我负责利润表预测及相关假设，将主要产品类别与 Services 分开建模，再结合毛利率、研发和销售管理费用、税率及股数假设，解释 FY2027—FY2032 收入与 EPS 的变化。工作簿保留 Revenue Build、Annual IS Forecast、IS Assumptions 及供后续预测使用的利润表输出。": "I prepared the income statement forecasts and assumptions, modelling major product categories and Services separately before applying margins, R&D, SG&A, taxation and share-count assumptions. The workbook retains Revenue Build, Annual IS Forecast, IS Assumptions and income statement outputs for subsequent forecasts. The analysis explains revenue and EPS changes over FY2027–FY2032.", "在小组估值框架中明确个人贡献": "An individual contribution within the group valuation framework", "最终成果为英文小组报告及 Excel 模型，涵盖股权现金流折现、剩余收益、相对估值与市场比较。我的工作集中于利润表预测及其假设，资产负债表预测、整体估值和建议由团队各部分共同支持。网站保留原始提交文件，报告中的 HOLD 为该课程案例在其研究时点和假设下的小组结论。": "The final English report and Excel model cover discounted flow to equity, residual income, relative valuation and market comparisons. My contribution centres on income statement forecasts and assumptions; balance sheet projections, valuation and recommendations are supported by the team’s combined work. Original submission files are retained. HOLD is the group’s course-case conclusion at the report’s research date and under its stated assumptions.", "财务预测": "Financial forecasting", "股权估值": "Equity valuation", "收入驱动": "Revenue drivers", "敏感性分析": "Sensitivity analysis", "英文估值报告 · 14 页（公开版）": "Valuation report (English) · 14 pages (public copy)", "财务预测与估值模型 · 15 个工作表": "Forecast & valuation model · 15 worksheets", "以收入驱动和利润率假设构建苹果财务预测，连接股权估值、敏感性分析与市场比较。": "Forecasting Apple from revenue drivers and margins, connecting equity valuation, sensitivity analysis and market comparisons."};
